\f0\fs24 \cf0 # README ------------------------------------------------------------------------\
# Generated on: 2026-10-23, updated on 2026-11-07\
\
# GENERAL INFORMATION -----------------------------------------------------------\
# Title of Analysis: Not Only Extremes: How Moderate Rainfall Deficits Affect Child Health in Mexico\
# MS Thesis\
# Author: Zachary Serby\
# Institution: Cornell University\
\
# SHARING / ACCESS INFORMATION --------------------------------------------------\
# Data sources:\
#   - Mexican Family Life Survey: MxFLS-1 (2002), MxFLS-2 (2005-06), MxFLS-3\
#     (2009-12). Data, codebooks and questionnaires from ennvih-mxfls.org.\
#   - CHIRPS v2.0 monthly precipitation, 0.05 degree grid (UCSB Climate Hazards Center).\
#   - INEGI Marco Geoestadistico 2010 municipal boundaries (Municipios_2010_5).\
#   - WHO Child Growth Standards (igrowup) and 2007 Growth Reference (who2007)\
#     Stata macros.\
\
# HOW TO RUN --------------------------------------------------------------------\
#   1. Open Scripts/00_Master.do by double-clicking it (or cd to the project or Scripts\
#      folder first). The project root is found automatically, so no paths need to\
#      change on a new computer. Check global Rscript, and the run_* switches (1 runs\
#      a step, all are on).\
#   2. Run it. The steps run in this order: rainfall (R), MxFLS cleaning 2002, 2005,\
#      2009 (later waves read earlier ones), DID analysis data, summary stats,\
#      drought map (R), DID/DDD, continuous DID (R), subanalyses by sex and by rural\
#      vs urban (Stata, then R), regression tables, results document (R).\
#   3. The rainfall step reads the 7.7 GB CHIRPS file, and its output is already in\
#      Data/Cleaned, so run_R can stay 0. If that file is missing (e.g. Data/Cleaned\
#      was deleted), the master runs the rainfall step anyway. The continuous DID\
#      steps are slow because of the wild cluster bootstrap.\
#\
# Reproducibility: set.seed(1234) before every bootstrap in R.\
\
# DATA & FILE OVERVIEW ----------------------------------------------------------\
# Scripts/\
#   - 00_Master.do : runs everything in order.\
#   - MS Thesis.Rproj : R project. The R scripts take the project root as one folder\
#     up from Scripts.\
#   - .Rprofile : saves the R console history to Output/Logs/Miscellaneous/R.Rhistory\
#     when R closes (replacing the last one), so no .Rhistory files are left in the folders.\
#   - Cleaning/ : Cleaned_rainfall_municipality_drought.R (CHIRPS to a\
#     municipality-year May-October rainfall panel with z-scores and a drought indicator), the\
#     Cleaning Script for MxFLS_2002_03.do, _2005_06.do and _2009_12.do (clean each\
#     wave, WHO z-scores and controls, the 2009 script appends the panel), and\
#     Build_DID_Analysis_Data.do (merges the panel and the rainfall on the child's\
#     2005 municipality and builds the treatment, controls and samples).\
#   - Statistics/ : Summary Stats DID.do (summary statistics, sample sizes and\
#     attrition tables, and the balance table and overlap figure of the rainfall\
#     classes), Regression Stats.do (all regression tables) and\
#     Drought_map.R (maps of the 2009 drought by municipality).\
#   - Regressions/ : DID_Regs.do (DID, DDD, event studies, robustness),\
#     Contdid_regs.R (continuous DID, SPI drought classes, remittances), functions.R\
#     (used by the R scripts), and the Subanalysis_Gender_* and Subanalysis_Rural_*\
#     versions of both. Their event studies use each subsample's Model 3 children, and the\
#     DDD event studies its Model 5 children with the event study controls, as in DID_Regs.do.\
#   - Paper/Build_Results.R : writes and compiles Paper/Paper.tex (the paper with its\
#     appendix), Paper/Online_Appendix.tex (the separate online appendix) and Paper/Results.tex\
#     (every table and figure). The text is in Paper/Text, where each %%TABLE or %%FIGURE line\
#     is replaced by that table or figure from Output.\
#     Citations and the reference list come from Paper/Text/References.bib in Chicago\
#     17th edition author-date style (biblatex-chicago, run with biber; TinyTeX installs both\
#     if they are missing). References.bib is exported from the Zotero Thesis collection with\
#     Better BibTeX (Better BibLaTeX, keep updated), so the build runs without Zotero. In the\
#     online appendix, a citation opens that entry in the reference list of Paper.pdf.\
#\
# Data/Raw/ (never edited by any script): MxFLS data and documentation (codebooks,\
#   questionnaires, user guides), CHIRPS, INEGI shapefiles, WHO macros.\
# Data/Cleaned/ (produced by the scripts):\
#   - MxFLS/ : wave files, mxfls_panel_2002_2005_2009.dta, mxfls_did_analysis.dta.\
#   - WHO_zscores/ : z-score files written by the WHO macros.\
#   - Rainfall/ : municipality_year_rainfall.dta.\
#\
# Output/ : Figures and Tables follow where things are placed: Main (paper), Appendix\
#   (appendix within the paper) and Online_Appendix (separate online appendix and everything\
#   else). Logs and Regression_Estimates have Main, Appendix and Miscellaneous.\
#   - Tables/Main : summary_stats_did_table.tex (discrete-dose samples), regression_tables_main.tex\
#     (discrete dose groups, BMIZ, HAZ and WAZ binary DID, continuous DID and remittances) and\
#     balance_table.tex (BMIZ balance of the dose groups, landscape).\
#   - Tables/Appendix : summary_stats_model3_table.tex (Model 3 samples) and\
#     regression_tables_appendix.tex (Model 3 with all covariates, all three waves, event studies).\
#   - Tables/Online_Appendix : sample_size_attrition_tables.tex, regression_tables_online_appendix.tex\
#     (subanalyses by sex and rural vs urban) and balance_table_online_appendix.tex (HAZ and WAZ).\
#   - Regression_Estimates/ : event study coefficients (.dta) and continuous DID csv files.\
#   - Figures/ : trends_*, event_study_*, contdid_*, drought_map_* and overlap_pscore_* (.png).\
#     Main has the dose level map, the dose event studies of all three outcomes, the BMIZ dose\
#     event study of children in all three waves (_all3) and the BMIZ overlap figure.\
#     Appendix has the binary drought map, the binary event studies with controls (_controls)\
#     on the Model 3 children, and the HAZ and WAZ dose event studies of children in all three waves.\
#     Dose event studies use the discrete-dose table children, and its pre-trend p-values come from them.\
#     Everything else, including the continuous dose figures and the subanalysis figures,\
#     is in Online_Appendix.\
#   - Logs/ : every log, and nowhere else.\
#\
# Paper/ : Paper.tex and Paper.pdf (the paper and its appendix), Online_Appendix.tex and\
#   Online_Appendix.pdf (separate online appendix), Results.tex and Results.pdf (every table\
#   and figure) and Text/ (the written text the paper and online appendix are built from).\
\
# DATA-SPECIFIC INFORMATION -----------------------------------------------------\
# mxfls_panel_2002_2005_2009.dta: 111,841 person-wave rows, 101 variables.\
#   - IDs: pid_link_canonical (person across waves), folio_canonical (household),\
#     wave, cvegeo (5-digit INEGI code, state + municipality).\
#   - Outcomes: haz, waz, bmiz (WHO z-scores).\
#   - remittance_hh: household got cash from a parent, sibling or child outside the\
#     household in the last 12 months, 1 = Yes 0 = No, missing if unresolved.\
#   - progresa_hh: household in Oportunidades aka PROGRESA in the last 12 months\
#     (Book II IN01 A1), 2002 only, 1 = Yes 0 = No, missing if DK. Used only in the\
#     robustness checks, not in the regressions.\
#   - int_date, int_year, int_month: measurement date (Book S, else Book C).\
#\
# mxfls_did_analysis.dta: the panel, wave renamed year, plus cvegeo05, droughts and\
#   rain_z 2002-2009, treat2009, rain_deficit2009, post, the _02 and _05 controls,\
#   progresa_hh_02, pc_expend_month_02 (2002 expenditure in pesos, balance table only)\
#   and the samples s_*, e_* and reg_*.\
#\
# municipality_year_rainfall.dta: 2,456 municipalities x 2001-2013.\
\
# SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS ---------------------------------------------------------\
#   - Stata. reghdfe, ftools, require, estout, distinct and boottest install automatically.\
#   - R >= 4.x. terra, sf, data.table, readxl, haven, did (>= 2.5.0), BMisc,\
#     sandwich, RColorBrewer and tinytex install automatically. contdid 0.1.1 installs from\
#     GitHub (bcallaway11/contdid) and needs ptetools >= 1.0.1. fwildclusterboot\
#     0.13.0 and summclust 0.7.2 install from the CRAN archive and need the Xcode\
#     command line tools and gfortran on a Mac.\
#   - TinyTeX compiles Paper.pdf, Online_Appendix.pdf and Results.pdf. Build_Results.R installs it if there is no LaTeX,\
#     and missing LaTeX packages (e.g. pdflscape) install automatically.\
#\
# END OF README ----------------------------------------------------------------}